/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::getAnimationPose()
\brief Copy the fully evaluated pose.

Refreshes the current pose, including persistent overrides and controllers, and returns an owned snapshot. Editing or retaining it does not affect the Sprite. A getter may reevaluate modifiers with deltaSeconds equal to zero.

\return An independent snapshot described below.

\note Call enableAnimationPose() successfully before using this method. Inside a modifier, use view.copy() instead of querying the Sprite.

\par Example
\code{.js}
const pose = sprite.getAnimationPose();
const hand = pose.bones.find(bone => bone.name === 'hand');
console.log(hand.rotation);
\endcode

\htmlonly[block]
<div class="shared-api-options">
\endhtmlonly

\anchor animation_pose_snapshot
\par Pose snapshot fields
| Field | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| `rigRevision` | Rig identity as a decimal string; compare before reusing cached bone or binding IDs. |
| `bones` | Array in bone-ID order. Each entry has `name`, `parent` (index or null), and the six parent-local transform fields below. |
| `bindings` | Array in binding-ID order. Each entry has `name`, `parent` (bone index or null), `kind` (image 0, point 1, box 2), and the six parent-local transform fields. |
| `variables` | Array of `{object, name, type, value}` records. An empty object name selects entity metadata. Types are float 0, integer 1, and string 2. |
| `tags` | Array of `{object, tags}` records, where tags is an array of strings. An empty object name selects entity tags. |

| Transform field | Units / meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `x`, `y` | Position in parent-local distance units. |
| `rotation` | Clockwise angle in radians. |
| `scaleX`, `scaleY` | Dimensionless axis scales; may include reflection. |
| `alpha` | Opacity from 0 to 1. |

Declared variable defaults are used when a clip has no matching track. Missing tag tracks produce empty sets. During a blend, string variables and tags switch at the halfway point. Undeclared variables are absent.

\htmlonly[block]
</div>
\endhtmlonly

\see sampleAnimationPose(), getAnimationBoneTransform()
*/
